  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Anaphylm, a sublingual epinephrine film, is the key value driver, targeting the anaphylaxis market. FDA alignment has cleared a path to NDA resubmission in Q3 2026, with international filings in Canada, EU, and UK also planned. Pipeline diversification advanced with a safe Phase 1 in androgenic alopecia. The underlying business shows momentum: revenue sharing with RTW was extended, and revenue growth is strong, signaling platform demand.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** The team secured a $150 million debt facility from Oaktree, providing non-dilutive runway through Anaphylm’s launch. They met 2025 targets and reaffirmed 2026 milestones, demonstrating reliability. Simultaneously pursuing multiple regulatory pathways and extending partnership terms illustrates efficient capital allocation. This disciplined execution has improved financial footing and investor sentiment.",
